Flayr Tune patch for JUCE 8.0.16-security (ea77444750de45e036e0279bb0291144bf8e3688).

MemoryBlock::fromBase64Encoding reads "<byte count>.<chars>" and allocated the
count as given before reading a character: "-1.AAAA" asked for SIZE_MAX
(std::bad_alloc escaping into the host), "2000000000.A" for 2 GB, and a long
number overflowed getIntValue. Every caller is affected, including
ValueTree::fromXml (any attribute named "base64:<x>" is decoded this way) and
the LV2 wrapper's session state, both of which run before a plug-in can check
anything. Accept only plain digits, at most INT_MAX, and at most what the
characters after the dot can encode.

Applied by CMakeLists.txt via FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND.

Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_core/memory/juce_MemoryBlock.cpp FLAYR_PATCH juce-base64-declared-size

